---
title: "create_obligation (Scallop Lend: Borrowing)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: user calls create_obligation()
    q_init --> q_check_accounts: count = get_obligation_count(user_address)
    q_check_accounts --> q_error: count >= 5
    q_check_accounts --> q_create: count < 5
    q_error --> [*]: revert "max sub-accounts reached"
    q_create --> q_mint_key: obligation = new Obligation(user_address)
    q_mint_key --> q_store: obligation_key = new ObligationKey(obligation.id)
    q_store --> [*]: transfer(obligation_key, user_address)

    note right of q_check_accounts
        INV-001: Each address can hold at most 5 obligations (1 primary + 4 sub-accounts)
        INV-002: obligation_key.obligation_id == obligation.id (key-obligation binding)
    end note

    note right of q_mint_key
        INV-003: Every Obligation has exactly one ObligationKey minted at creation
        INV-004: ObligationKey is transferable (NFT-like ownership token)
    end note
